Given below are two statements:&nbsp;
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td><span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>Statement I:</strong></span></td><td><span id="cke_bm_277S" style="display: none;">&nbsp;</span>The primary&nbsp;<span class="math-tex">\(CO_2\)</span>&nbsp;acceptor in&nbsp;<span class="math-tex">\(C_4\)</span>&nbsp;plants is phosphoenolpyruvate and is found in the mesophyll cells.&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td><span style="white-space:nowrap;"><strong>Statement II:</strong></span></td><td><span id="cke_bm_458S" style="display: none;">&nbsp;</span>Mesophyll cells in&nbsp;<span class="math-tex">\(C_4\)</span>&nbsp;plants lack RuBisCO&nbsp;enzyme.</td></tr></tbody></table>
In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :&nbsp;

<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td>1.</td><td><strong>Statement I</strong> is incorrect but <strong>Statement II </strong>is correct.</td></tr><tr><td>2.</td><td>Both <strong>Statement I </strong>and <strong>Statement II </strong>are correct.</td></tr><tr><td>3.</td><td>Both <strong>Statement I </strong>and <strong>Statement II&nbsp; </strong>are incorrect.</td></tr><tr><td>4.</td><td><strong>Statement I </strong>is correct but <strong>Statement II </strong>is incorrect.</td></tr></tbody></table>
